      nonprofit Center for Open Science that has a mission to increase openness, 
      integrity, and reproducibility of research. KSC is an employee of ASAPbio, which 
      is a scientist-driven non-profit promoting transparency and innovation in life 
      science communication, and she was previously a paid consultant of the Center for 
      Open Science. VB is editor-in-chief of the Medical Journal of Australia, co-chair 
      of DORA, and a former chair of COPE. CL is on the Board of Directors for Rapid 
      Science and previously served on the Board of Directors for ASAPbio. D. Moher is 
      developing an extension to TOP for academic institutions. EM-W received previous 
      support for research about the TOP Guidelines from Arnold Ventures (formerly the 
      Laura and John Arnold Foundation). THP has led a project that received grant 
      support (from the Laura and John Arnold Foundation and NSF award number DEB - 
      1548207) to promote the adoption of the TOP guidelines in ecology and 
      evolutionary biology, and has served in leadership positions in SORTEE, an 
      organization devoted to promoting open, reliable, and transparent ecology and 
      evolutionary biology. SG is the Methodological Transparency Editor at Journal of 
      Research on Educational Effectiveness, has received previous support for research 
      about the TOP Guidelines from Arnold Ventures (formerly the Laura and John Arnold 
      Foundation), and has received honoraria in the last three years from the Berkeley 
      Initiative for Transparency in the Social Sciences, Federation of American 
      Scientists, International Initiative for Impact Evaluation, Society for Research 
      on Educational Effectiveness, and University of South Dakota. IH is an employee 
      of PLOS, which publishes open access journals, and is responsible for promoting 
      the adoption of Open Science practices and policies. DU serves as the protocol 
      editor for Systematic Reviews, a journal under Springer Nature. MLR has received 
      funding from the Medical Library Association and the Baltic-American Freedom 
      Foundation to teach about the PRISMA-S reporting guideline, for which she was the 
      lead author, and received the NINDS Rigor Champions Prize for her work promoting 
      research reproducibility. ML serves in leadership positions in SORTEE, an 
      organization devoted to promoting open, reliable, and transparent ecology and 
      evolutionary biology. The remaining authors have nothing to declare.
